  "id": "image_qwen_image_2_1_image_edit",
  "name": "Qwen Image 2.1 — image edit with references",
  "description": "Edit a picture by describing the change, and hand the model up to ten reference pictures to work from.\n\nRefer to them in the prompt as <image1>, <image2>, <image3>… — that is how Qwen addresses them. Image 1 is the picture being edited; the rest are references, and every one of them is optional. Typical uses: put the garment from <image2> onto the person in <image1>; restyle <image1> in the look of <image2>; drop the object from <image2> into the scene of <image1>.\n\nSay what must STAY as clearly as what changes — \"keep the pose, the face, the background and the lighting\" — otherwise the model reinterprets more than you wanted. The result follows the size and aspect of image 1.\n\nA reference slot you leave empty is removed from the graph completely, so an unused slot can never influence the picture.",
  "category": "image-edit",
  "tags": [
    "qwen",
    "qwen-image",
    "2.1",
    "image-edit",
    "reference",
    "multi-image"
  ],
